1
00:00:02,222 --> 00:00:07,217
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,725
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:12,357
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:12,862 --> 00:00:14,057
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:14,658 --> 00:00:21,348
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

6
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:23,483
السلام وعليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

7
00:00:24,534 --> 00:00:26,989
When Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه was in Yemen,

8
00:00:27,386 --> 00:00:34,182
 there were some rumors surrounding his authority as an Ameer(أمير) over there.

9
00:00:35,248 --> 00:00:38,674
Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه had some camels of Sadaqah(صدقه) with him

10
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:43,712
and the members of his army, they wanted to use these camels for transport.

11
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:45,857
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي بن أبي طالب) refused.

12
00:00:46,285 --> 00:00:48,024
And he had some work to do.

13
00:00:48,064 --> 00:00:53,479
So, he left deputy to take care of affairs in his absence.

14
00:00:53,519 --> 00:00:59,227
And when he came back, he found out that the camels were used for transport

15
00:00:59,251 --> 00:01:01,688
because he saw the marks of the saddles on them.

16
00:01:01,944 --> 00:01:08,132
And he also saw that the people were wearing some of the garments that were also given as part of Sadaqah(صدقه).

17
00:01:08,876 --> 00:01:13,489
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) became very angry, and he ordered that they take off those garments,

18
00:01:13,545 --> 00:01:18,025
and they give them back and that caused some rumors.

19
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:22,368
And someone went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ to report what happened

20
00:01:22,408 --> 00:01:25,557
 and there was one of the Sahabah(صحابه) that was there,

21
00:01:25,597 --> 00:01:30,029
and when this man was reporting these things against Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

22
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:32,898
the other Sahabi(صحابي) was saying: Yes, that's right.! Yes, that's right.!

23
00:01:33,375 --> 00:01:38,892
And this Sahabi(صحابي) used to say that I used to dislike Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), I used to hate him.

24
00:01:39,279 --> 00:01:42,426
And Rasool Allah ﷺ when he saw him saying: Yes, that's right,

25
00:01:42,466 --> 00:01:46,586
approving the complaints that were against Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

26
00:01:47,287 --> 00:01:53,491
Rasool Allah ﷺ put his hand on the knee of this Sahabi(صحابي) and he told him;

27
00:01:53,689 --> 00:01:54,886
Do you dislike Ali(علي)?

28
00:01:54,973 --> 00:01:55,971
He said: Yes.

29
00:01:56,225 --> 00:01:58,241
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: You should love him.

30
00:01:58,606 --> 00:02:04,505
So, this Sahabi(صحابي) said after that, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was among the most beloved to me.

31
00:02:05,447 --> 00:02:07,357
So, this was the situation.

32
00:02:07,405 --> 00:02:12,319
So when Rasool Allah ﷺ was returning from Hajjat-Ul-Widaa(حجةالوداع).

33
00:02:12,761 --> 00:02:15,025
And he arrived in a place called Ghadeer Khumr(غدير خمر).

34
00:02:15,787 --> 00:02:20,259
Rasool Allah ﷺ gathered the people and delivered to them the famous statement.

35
00:02:20,812 --> 00:02:23,353
مَنْ كُنْت مَوْلَاهُ فِعْلِيٌّ مَوْلاهُ

36
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:30,193
If I am the friend of someone, then Ali(علي) is also his friend.

37
00:02:30,704 --> 00:02:37,878
Mola(مولا) is friend, protector, close associate, so all of these statements to apply to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

38
00:02:37,909 --> 00:02:42,163
Now, the Shia(شيعه) they carried this too far and they took it out of the context.

39
00:02:42,246 --> 00:02:44,116
The context of what happened is that

40
00:02:44,275 --> 00:02:47,458
there were false rumors going against Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

41
00:02:47,498 --> 00:02:53,689
so Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to defend the reputation of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) in front of everyone

42
00:02:54,146 --> 00:02:57,094
and to let everyone know the status of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

43
00:02:57,563 --> 00:02:59,724
being the cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

44
00:03:00,070 --> 00:03:10,191
the husband of his daughter and the father of the only lineage remaining from Rasool Allah ﷺ

45
00:03:10,215 --> 00:03:15,405
because no lineage remained from Rasool Allah ﷺ except through Al-Hassan Wal Hussain(ألحسن والحُسين),

46
00:03:15,658 --> 00:03:18,847
the grandchildren of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

47
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:22,582
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling the people that

48
00:03:22,694 --> 00:03:26,682
if I am your Mola(مولا) than Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is also your Mola(مولا).

49
00:03:27,201 --> 00:03:30,704
If you love me, then you need to love Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

50
00:03:30,973 --> 00:03:34,200
Rasool Allah ﷺ returned to Madina.

51
00:03:34,652 --> 00:03:41,539
And now we're entering into the 11th year of Hijrah(هجرى) spent there the month of Muharram(محرم).

52
00:03:41,579 --> 00:03:47,849
And in Safar(صفر), Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) to lead an army

53
00:03:48,274 --> 00:03:52,819
that is to be sent to the land of Balqaa(بلقاء) in Ash-Sham(الشام).

54
00:03:53,454 --> 00:03:55,970
And the instructions were for Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد);

55
00:03:56,315 --> 00:04:00,012
To step with his horses on the land where his father was killed.

56
00:04:00,052 --> 00:04:06,624
So, you can see now, that the focus of Rasool Allah ﷺ is on the boundaries with the Roman Empire.

57
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:09,234
You have Mo'ta(مؤته) first and then you have the Tabook(تبوك).

58
00:04:09,296 --> 00:04:12,320
And now you have this army of Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد),

59
00:04:12,374 --> 00:04:16,122
in addition to the Sarayah(سراية) that were also sent into that area.

60
00:04:16,946 --> 00:04:18,617
So, this happened in Safar(صفر).

61
00:04:18,657 --> 00:04:21,006
Now, Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) at that time, how old was he?

62
00:04:21,371 --> 00:04:25,425
He was between 18 to 20 years old, very young.

63
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:29,521
And you have seniors Sahabah(صحابه) from Al-Muhajireen(ألمهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار),

64
00:04:29,704 --> 00:04:36,083
older men with much experience in warfare and in leadership, and managing the affairs of armies

65
00:04:36,321 --> 00:04:42,482
and Rasool Allah ﷺ appoints a very young man to lead an army that included Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Umar(عمر).

66
00:04:43,041 --> 00:04:45,088
So, there was some talk going on.

67
00:04:45,128 --> 00:04:50,750
And now, see the community is large for so there's more room for idle talk to go on,

68
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:55,694
because you still had a strong presence of Nifaq(نفاق) and large number of Muslims.

69
00:04:55,734 --> 00:04:57,740
So, there was talk going around.

70
00:04:57,941 --> 00:05:00,084
Why is Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) appointed?

71
00:05:00,767 --> 00:05:03,066
For two reasons the objections were two reasons,

72
00:05:03,106 --> 00:05:03,867
Number one, his age

73
00:05:03,907 --> 00:05:06,962
and Number two, that he belongs to the slave caste.

74
00:05:06,986 --> 00:05:11,002
I mean, his father was a former slave and his mother's same thing, Umm Aimen(أم أيمن).

75
00:05:11,441 --> 00:05:15,588
Therefore, how could he lead over the free men?

76
00:05:15,804 --> 00:05:20,029
And these concerns reach to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

77
00:05:20,053 --> 00:05:23,450
So, Rasool Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه said, and this is in Bukhari(ألبخاري)

78
00:05:23,661 --> 00:05:28,409
إنْ تَطْعَنُوا في إمارَتِهِ فقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تطَعَنون في إمارَةِ أبِيهِ مِن قَبْلِهِ،

79
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,831
If you are disputing his appointment,

80
00:05:31,117 --> 00:05:34,234
then you have disputed the appointment of his father before.

81
00:05:34,463 --> 00:05:41,341
وَاَيْمُ اللَّهِ لقَدْ كانَ خَلِيقًا لِلْإِمارَةِ، وإنْ كانَ مِن أحَبِّ النَّاسِ إلَيَّ، وإنَّ هذا لَمِنْ أحَبِّ النَّاسِ إلَيَّ بَعْدَهُ

82
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:46,329
And In the name of Allah, and now he's talking about his father, Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثة).

83
00:05:46,424 --> 00:05:51,895
He was suitable person for appointing as a leader,

84
00:05:52,223 --> 00:05:54,834
and he was one of the most beloved people to me.

85
00:05:55,191 --> 00:05:59,277
And this man is one of the most beloved people to me, after him.

86
00:05:59,591 --> 00:06:04,663
So, Osamah(اسامه), Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying that he took the position of his father after his father passed away.

87
00:06:05,178 --> 00:06:06,788
In the month of Safar(صفر).

88
00:06:07,304 --> 00:06:11,372
The beginning of the end was starting.

89
00:06:12,236 --> 00:06:19,958
Rasool Allah ﷺ has received many Ayaat(آيات) and indications that he would die just like every other human being.

90
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:26,920
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed Ayaat(آيات) that warn, of the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

91
00:06:27,147 --> 00:06:31,275
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says; And this was revealed in Makkah.

92
00:06:31,623 --> 00:06:36,023
وَلَلْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لَكَ مِنَ الْأُولَىٰ۝

93
00:06:36,356 --> 00:06:40,751
وَلَسَوْفَ يُعْطِيكَ رَبُّكَ فَتَرْضَىَٰ۝

94
00:06:41,163 --> 00:06:44,625
And the Hereafter is better for you than the first life

95
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:48,660
and your Lord is going to give you and you will be satisfied.

96
00:06:49,709 --> 00:06:55,127
And therefore, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was given the choice of living in Duniyah(دنيا) or dying,

97
00:06:55,504 --> 00:06:57,276
we will see what his choice was?

98
00:06:57,779 --> 00:07:03,048
Because he has the promise from very early on in Makkah, that the afterlife is better for you.

99
00:07:03,547 --> 00:07:07,635
And Allah will give you until you're satisfied and Allah سبحانه وتعالى says:

100
00:07:07,897 --> 00:07:16,033
إِنَّكَ مَيِّتٌ وَإِنَّهُمْ مَيِّتُونَ ۝

101
00:07:16,239 --> 00:07:24,917
ثُمَّ إِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ تَخْتَصِمُونَ۝

102
00:07:25,374 --> 00:07:27,646
Az-Zumar(إلزمر) Thirty-Thirty One(30-31);

103
00:07:27,853 --> 00:07:31,702
Indeed, you are to die and indeed they are to die,

104
00:07:32,053 --> 00:07:37,187
then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute.

105
00:07:37,621 --> 00:07:40,577
When Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Surah Al-Ambiyaa(سورة الانبياء).

106
00:07:40,737 --> 00:07:46,560
وَمَا جَعَلْنَا لِبَشَرٍ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ الْخُلْدَ

107
00:07:46,805 --> 00:07:51,001
 أَفَإِنْ مِتَّ فَهُمُ الْخَالِدُونَ۝

108
00:07:51,231 --> 00:07:58,674
 كُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَائِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ

109
00:07:59,173 --> 00:08:08,568
 وَنَبْلُوكُمْ بِالشَّرِّ وَالْخَيْرِ فِتْنَةً ۖ وَإِلَيْنَا تُرْجَعُونَ۝

110
00:08:08,949 --> 00:08:12,035
And we did not grant any man before you eternity.

111
00:08:12,386 --> 00:08:17,457
So, if you die, would they be eternal, every soul will taste death,

112
00:08:18,008 --> 00:08:23,880
and we test you with evil and with good as trial and to us, you will be returned.

113
00:08:24,430 --> 00:08:29,581
So, the whole life is just a trial of good and bad, and everyone will die.

114
00:08:30,202 --> 00:08:36,168
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed to Muhammadﷺ during the Hajj(حَجْ) of Widaa(وداع).

115
00:08:36,453 --> 00:08:46,277
اَلْيَوْمَ أَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِينَكُمْ وَأَتْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِي وَرَضِيتُ لَكُمُ الْإِسْلَامَ دِينًا۝

116
00:08:47,024 --> 00:08:52,705
This day, I have perfected for you, your religion and completed my favor upon you

117
00:08:53,327 --> 00:08:55,685
and have approved for you Islam as religion.

118
00:08:56,290 --> 00:09:00,333
Now there's nothing directly here that indicates the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ

119
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:03,578
but there is an indication of the fulfillment of the mission.

120
00:09:04,356 --> 00:09:05,468
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

121
00:09:05,956 --> 00:09:13,460
وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ

122
00:09:13,654 --> 00:09:20,093
أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَىٰ أَعْقَابِكُمْ ۚ

123
00:09:20,291 --> 00:09:27,110
وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلَىٰ عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئًا

124
00:09:27,376 --> 00:09:31,039
وَسَيَجْزِي اللَّهُ الشَّاكِرِينَ ۝

125
00:09:31,229 --> 00:09:39,678
وَمَا كَانَ لِنَفْسٍ أَنْ تَمُوتَ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ كِتَابًا مُؤَجَّلًا

126
00:09:39,947 --> 00:09:49,759
وَمَنْ يُرِدْ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا نُؤْتِهِ مِنْهَا وَمَنْ يُرِدْ ثَوَابَ الْآخِرَةِ نُؤْتِهِ مِنْهَا ۚ

127
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:53,663
وَسَنَجْزِي الشَّاكِرِينَ۝

128
00:09:54,394 --> 00:09:59,170
Muhammad(محمد) is not but the Messenger, other Messengers have passed on before him.

129
00:09:59,487 --> 00:10:04,633
So, if he was to die or be killed, would you turn back on your heels to unbelief,

130
00:10:05,302 --> 00:10:09,072
and he, who returns back on his heels will never harm Allah at all.

131
00:10:09,431 --> 00:10:11,134
But Allah will reward the Grateful.

132
00:10:11,785 --> 00:10:18,577
And it is not possible for one to die except by permission of Allah at a decree determined

133
00:10:18,974 --> 00:10:23,227
 and whoever desires the reward of this world, we will give him their off.

134
00:10:23,829 --> 00:10:28,171
And whoever desires the reward of the hereafter who will give him their off.

135
00:10:28,690 --> 00:10:30,976
And we will reward the Grateful.

136
00:10:31,302 --> 00:10:32,410
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

137
00:10:32,572 --> 00:10:37,430
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ۝

138
00:10:37,950 --> 00:10:42,637
 إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ۝

139
00:10:43,197 --> 00:10:50,370
وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا۝

140
00:10:50,961 --> 00:10:58,648
 فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا۝

141
00:10:59,764 --> 00:11:02,339
When the victory of Allah has come, and the conquest

142
00:11:03,025 --> 00:11:07,285
and you see the people entering into the religion of Allah in multitudes

143
00:11:07,742 --> 00:11:13,302
 then exalt Him, with praise of your Lord and ask forgiveness of Him.

144
00:11:13,686 --> 00:11:16,384
Indeed He is ever Accepting of repentance.

145
00:11:16,963 --> 00:11:22,225
Again in these Ayaat(آيات), there is no indication, there's no direct indication of the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

146
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:32,537
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) used to sit with the senior Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and Ansaar(أنصار) in the court of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

147
00:11:32,837 --> 00:11:37,433
So, some of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and Ansaar(أنصار) said, why is this young man sitting here,

148
00:11:37,775 --> 00:11:42,123
when we have sons in his age, and they're not invited?

149
00:11:42,415 --> 00:11:45,498
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted to point out to them, the reason.

150
00:11:45,688 --> 00:11:49,035
So, he asked them: What do you understand from this Surah(سورة)?

151
00:11:49,329 --> 00:11:50,662
 Everyone gave an answer,

152
00:11:50,776 --> 00:11:54,984
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) asked Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه what do you understand from it?

153
00:11:55,008 --> 00:11:56,858
He said: I understand from it, the death of Rasool Ullah.

154
00:11:57,670 --> 00:12:00,587
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: And that is what I understand from it.

155
00:12:00,612 --> 00:12:03,599
And he made a point to the Sahabah(صحابه), who were there

156
00:12:03,855 --> 00:12:07,840
that Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) is sitting with us now, because of his knowledge, because of his understanding,

157
00:12:07,865 --> 00:12:12,150
because of the Fiqh(فقه) and the deep understanding that he has of Islam

158
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:16,603
because this Surah(سورة) says; When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest

159
00:12:16,912 --> 00:12:22,206
and the victory of Allah is the end result of Da'wah(دعوة).

160
00:12:22,599 --> 00:12:24,279
So, it's towards the end.

161
00:12:24,692 --> 00:12:26,289
وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ۝

162
00:12:26,313 --> 00:12:28,129
The end result belongs to the believers.

163
00:12:28,446 --> 00:12:31,648
And you see the people entering into the religion of Allah in multitudes

164
00:12:31,711 --> 00:12:36,463
and that was what is happening after Fateh Makkah(فتح مكه), People were entering in multitudes.

165
00:12:37,056 --> 00:12:40,281
Then exalt Him with praise of your Lord and ask forgiveness of Him.

166
00:12:40,566 --> 00:12:47,194
We usually ask Allah for forgiveness, when after we do the deed, then we ask Allah to forgive us.

167
00:12:47,486 --> 00:12:49,089
So, after Salah(صلاة), what do you say.?

168
00:12:49,311 --> 00:12:51,578
استغفرالله, استغفرالله, استغفرالله

169
00:12:51,921 --> 00:12:54,066
after Hajj(حَجْ) same thing Astaghfirullah(استغفرالله).

170
00:12:54,230 --> 00:12:56,570
So, Astaghfaar(استغفار) is something that comes towards the end

171
00:12:56,610 --> 00:13:00,752
and this is an indication that the end of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ is near

172
00:13:01,474 --> 00:13:03,776
and Taubah(توبة) also comes towards the end.

173
00:13:04,422 --> 00:13:07,420
There are also some Ahadith(احاديث) we talked about the Hadith(حديث) where,

174
00:13:07,721 --> 00:13:10,189
when Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل) to Yemen

175
00:13:10,229 --> 00:13:13,535
and told him you might not meet me anymore, and Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل) cried.

176
00:13:14,515 --> 00:13:17,048
There is also the Hadith(حديث), where Rasool Allah ﷺ said in Hajj(حَجْ);

177
00:13:17,411 --> 00:13:21,093
لِتَأْخُذُواعَنِّيْ مَنَاسِكَكُمْ، فَلَعَلِّيْ لَااَحُجْ بعد عَامِيْ هَذَه

178
00:13:21,457 --> 00:13:24,401
Take from me your rituals, learn from me your rituals,

179
00:13:24,647 --> 00:13:27,939
because I may never make Hajj(حَجْ) again after this time.

180
00:13:28,732 --> 00:13:29,658
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

181
00:13:29,682 --> 00:13:38,194
إِنَّ جِبْرِيلَ كانَ يُعَارِضُنِي بالقُرْآنَ كُلَّ سَنَةٍ مَرَّةً، وإنَّه عَارَضَنِي به العَامَ مَرَّتَيْنِ، ولَا أُرَاهُ إلَّا اقتراب أجَلِي

182
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:39,632
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

183
00:13:39,672 --> 00:13:44,910
Jibril(جبريل) used to recite Qur'an with me, every year once, they would go through the whole Qur'an.

184
00:13:45,253 --> 00:13:47,161
 And this year, he did it twice.

185
00:13:47,361 --> 00:13:51,082
And I see that as an indication of the end of my life.

186
00:13:51,609 --> 00:13:55,702
So, in the month of Safar(صفر) of the year 11 of Al-Hijrah(ألهجرة).

187
00:13:56,308 --> 00:14:04,780
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent to Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومويهبة), a servant of Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

188
00:14:05,314 --> 00:14:07,665
And this was late at night,

189
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:12,938
so Rasool Allah ﷺ called, he woke up, Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومويهبة) and called him and told him;

190
00:14:13,213 --> 00:14:19,225
يَا أَبَا مُوَيْهِبَةَ إنِّيْ قَدْ أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أَسْتَغْفِرَ لِأَهْلِ هَذَا الْبَقِيَعْ فَانْطَلَقْ مَعِيْ

191
00:14:20,447 --> 00:14:28,093
O Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومو يهبة) I have been commanded to ask Allah to forgive, the people of Al-Baqiyah(البقيه), so come with me.

192
00:14:28,513 --> 00:14:30,913
 Al-Baqiyah(البقيه) is the cemetery of Madina,

193
00:14:31,316 --> 00:14:39,010
the blessed cemetery, where the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who struggled with him,

194
00:14:39,109 --> 00:14:41,924
fought with him, supported him, were buried

195
00:14:42,379 --> 00:14:47,890
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was ordered by Allah to go to the cemetery and ask Allah to forgive them.

196
00:14:48,772 --> 00:14:53,060
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومو يهبة) to go with him.

197
00:14:53,557 --> 00:14:59,601
So, they went together at night to Al-Baqiyah(البقيه) and when Rasool Allah ﷺ arrived there.

198
00:15:00,386 --> 00:15:03,279
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) Rasool Allah ﷺ was going in the middle of the night

199
00:15:04,228 --> 00:15:08,632
to the cemetery to give his Sahabah رضي الله عنهم a company.

200
00:15:09,010 --> 00:15:09,849
He told them;

201
00:15:10,277 --> 00:15:12,857
السلام عليكم يا اهل المقابر

202
00:15:13,714 --> 00:15:17,465
 Peace be upon you, O people of the graves.

203
00:15:18,405 --> 00:15:23,124
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, and look at these uplifting words for them.

204
00:15:23,538 --> 00:15:27,775
لِيَهْنَأ لَكُمْ مَا أَصَبَحْتُمْ فِيْهِ مِمَّا أَصْبَحَ النَّاسُ فِيْهِ

205
00:15:28,248 --> 00:15:29,770
Congratulations.

206
00:15:30,222 --> 00:15:36,031
Rasool Allah ﷺ is congratulating the people of this cemetery, the people, who are dead.

207
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:41,901
Congratulations! That you do not experienced, what people here are experiencing.

208
00:15:42,795 --> 00:15:47,865
Congratulations! That you passed away, in the early days of Da'wah(دعوة),

209
00:15:47,889 --> 00:15:51,577
when the hearts were pure and the people were together and they were unified.

210
00:15:52,362 --> 00:15:56,290
Congratulations! That you died in the difficult days when the rewards were great.

211
00:15:57,028 --> 00:16:02,116
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them that you are in a better position than who's left behind.

212
00:16:02,496 --> 00:16:04,090
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

213
00:16:04,453 --> 00:16:14,150
أَقْبَلَتْ اَلْفِتَنْ كَقِطْعَ اللَّيْلِ الْمُظْلِمْ، يَتْبَعُ آخِرُهَا أَوَّلَّهَا، وَالْآخِرَةُ شَرُّ مِّنَّ الْأُوْلَى

214
00:16:14,521 --> 00:16:21,816
Trials and tribulations come like dark portions of the night following each other in succession.

215
00:16:22,044 --> 00:16:24,087
The last been worse than the first.

216
00:16:25,036 --> 00:16:30,385
Trials and tribulations are on their way and we are living in that time dear brothers and sisters.

217
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:35,483
We are living in the times of trials and tribulations, we're living in a time of Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

218
00:16:35,823 --> 00:16:37,939
Fitnah(فِتْنَه) in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and Fitnah(فِتْنَه) in Deen(دين).

219
00:16:38,348 --> 00:16:43,158
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is congratulating, these Sahabah(صحابه), who died early and telling them,

220
00:16:43,337 --> 00:16:45,164
congratulations that you died early,

221
00:16:45,375 --> 00:16:49,926
because now the Fittan are coming like dark pieces of the night, one after the other.

222
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:53,637
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ looked at Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومو يهبة) and said;

223
00:16:54,046 --> 00:17:04,574
إِنِّيْ قَدْ أُعْطِيْتُ مَفَاتِيْحَ خَزَائِنِ الدُّنْيَا وَالْخُلْدَ فِيْهَا، ثُمَّ الْجَنَّةْ فَخُيِّرْتُ بَيْنَ ذَلِكَ وَبَيْنَ لِقَاءِ رَبِّيْ وَالْجَنَةْ

224
00:17:04,953 --> 00:17:06,723
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومويهبة)

225
00:17:07,143 --> 00:17:14,941
I was given the choice of the keys of the treasures of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and living in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) as long as it exists.

226
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,617
And then paradise, or

227
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:19,769
وَبَيْنَ لِقَاءِ رَبِّيْ وَالْجَنَةْ

228
00:17:19,793 --> 00:17:21,959
Meeting my Lord or paradise.

229
00:17:22,346 --> 00:17:27,256
So, the choice is you can live in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), as long as this world would survive,

230
00:17:27,635 --> 00:17:31,030
and you will be given the keys to the treasures of this world.

231
00:17:31,449 --> 00:17:36,256
And then when you pass away, you will be in paradise, that's choice number one.

232
00:17:36,514 --> 00:17:40,929
And the second choice is to meet Allah now and Jannah(جنة).

233
00:17:41,221 --> 00:17:44,084
Abu Mu'aihibbah(ابومو يهبة) said: Choose us.

234
00:17:44,529 --> 00:17:46,536
In one narration and in this narration he says;

235
00:17:46,708 --> 00:17:50,988
Choose the keys of the treasures and living in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) as long as it is living and then Jannah(جنة).

236
00:17:51,245 --> 00:17:57,023
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No! I have chosen to meet Allah and paradise.

237
00:17:57,578 --> 00:18:03,125
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ sought forgiveness for the people of Al-Baqiyyah(البقيه) and then he left.

238
00:18:03,988 --> 00:18:08,732
And when he arrived home the illness of his death began.

239
00:18:09,095 --> 00:18:11,437
Rasool Allah ﷺ was not attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

240
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:16,239
Rasool Allah ﷺ his concern in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) was his Ummah(امة),

241
00:18:16,577 --> 00:18:21,101
his concern was not building, it was not wealth.

242
00:18:21,394 --> 00:18:29,204
He didn't have attachment to Ad-Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and therefore Ibn Kathir رضي الله عنه, He says;

243
00:18:29,229 --> 00:18:34,587
فَاِنَّ الدُّنْيَا بِحاذَفِرِهَا كَانَتْ اَحْقَرَعِنْدَه’ كَمَا هِيَ عِنْدَالله ،

244
00:18:34,817 --> 00:18:39,249
مِنْ اَنْ يَسْعی لَهَا اَوْ يُتْرُكْهَا بَعْدَه’ مِيْرَاثًا صَلَوَاتُ الله وَسَلَامُ عَلَيْه

245
00:18:39,987 --> 00:18:48,386
He said; The Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) was so small in the eyes of Rasool Allah ﷺ and it is also small in the eyes of Allah

246
00:18:48,457 --> 00:18:53,413
 that Rasool Allah ﷺ left it, without leaving behind anything.

247
00:18:53,875 --> 00:18:56,176
Ayesha رضي الله عنها was saying,

248
00:18:56,279 --> 00:18:57,823
وَ رَاْسَى، وَرَاْسَى

249
00:18:58,601 --> 00:19:01,506
My head hurts, My head hurts.

250
00:19:01,903 --> 00:19:03,149
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

251
00:19:03,173 --> 00:19:04,499
بَلْ اَنَا ، وَرَاْسَه

252
00:19:04,523 --> 00:19:08,347
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No! It is me, who should say, my head hurts.

253
00:19:08,994 --> 00:19:14,655
Rasool Allah ﷺ was having a severe headache and he was also having a severe fever

254
00:19:15,511 --> 00:19:19,660
and the fever was so severe on Rasool Allah ﷺ,

255
00:19:20,114 --> 00:19:22,960
when one of the companions put his hand on Rasool Ullah, he said;

256
00:19:23,399 --> 00:19:26,096
I cannot leave my hand on you because of the heat.

257
00:19:26,136 --> 00:19:30,723
I mean, it was very uncomfortable to touch the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ because of his fever

258
00:19:31,602 --> 00:19:33,716
and the companion told Rasool Allah ﷺ;

259
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:35,718
انك لتوعك وعكا شديدا

260
00:19:35,886 --> 00:19:39,216
You are going through very severe illness.

261
00:19:39,436 --> 00:19:41,128
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

262
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:47,208
That is because we, the Prophets suffer double the suffering of everyone else.

263
00:19:48,117 --> 00:19:49,837
Because Allahعَزّوجَلّ loves them.

264
00:19:50,321 --> 00:19:52,805
Allahعَزّوجَلّ puts them through tougher tests,

265
00:19:53,162 --> 00:19:56,102
because they are stronger and greater and better.

266
00:19:56,333 --> 00:19:58,960
Allahعَزّوجَلّ puts them through tougher tests.

267
00:19:59,712 --> 00:20:02,979
Rasool Allah ﷺ, one day wanted to go to the Masjid(مسجد)

268
00:20:03,131 --> 00:20:04,580
لَعَلِّيْ اَحَدٌ عَلَى النَّاسْ

269
00:20:04,605 --> 00:20:07,395
He wanted to give a covenant to the people.

270
00:20:07,633 --> 00:20:12,337
So, he said gather for me seven buckets of water from seven different wells

271
00:20:12,548 --> 00:20:15,841
and pour them on me, so that I can go out to the people.

272
00:20:16,564 --> 00:20:23,572
So, they brought him this water and they were pouring this cold water on the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ to cool it down

273
00:20:23,627 --> 00:20:24,808
because of the temperature

274
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:29,002
and to give Rasool Allah ﷺ the ability to go out to the Masjid(مسجد).

275
00:20:29,749 --> 00:20:32,005
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ was carried to the Masjid(مسجد).

276
00:20:32,502 --> 00:20:35,642
Where his head was wrapped because of his headache.

277
00:20:36,177 --> 00:20:39,464
And he had to lean, he couldn't walk so he had to lean,

278
00:20:39,835 --> 00:20:43,911
on one of the sons of Al-Abbas(العباس) and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to take him to the Masjid(مسجد).

279
00:20:44,671 --> 00:20:48,585
And his feet were dragging on the ground because he couldn't lift them up.

280
00:20:49,237 --> 00:20:52,633
And he went to the Masjid(مسجد) and he gave a Naseeha(نصيحه).

281
00:20:53,114 --> 00:20:59,530
After praising Allahعَزّوجَلّ, Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned the Shuhadaa(شهداء) of Uhud(أحَد),

282
00:21:00,316 --> 00:21:01,715
and asked Allah to forgive them.

283
00:21:02,430 --> 00:21:10,455
Notice here, Rasool Allah ﷺ, went to Al-Baqiyah(البقيه) to ask Allah to forgive the Muslims, who died in Al-Baqiyah(البقيه)

284
00:21:10,828 --> 00:21:14,400
and now Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking forgiveness to the Shuhadaa(شهداء) of Uhud(أحَد).

285
00:21:14,958 --> 00:21:20,859
This shows us, the loyalty that Rasool Allah ﷺ had to his companions,

286
00:21:21,152 --> 00:21:24,821
the love that he had for them and remembrance is that he had for them.

287
00:21:25,247 --> 00:21:27,454
Rasool Allah ﷺ was concerned about his Ummah(امة) .

288
00:21:27,849 --> 00:21:29,791
Rasool Allah ﷺ lived for us,

289
00:21:29,958 --> 00:21:31,505
he lived for me and you,

290
00:21:31,823 --> 00:21:33,902
he gave his life for me and you,

291
00:21:34,227 --> 00:21:34,976
he struggled,

292
00:21:35,046 --> 00:21:36,204
he went through difficulties,

293
00:21:36,244 --> 00:21:37,282
he suffered poverty,

294
00:21:37,322 --> 00:21:38,345
he suffered pain,

295
00:21:38,872 --> 00:21:39,976
he had to fight,

296
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:46,158
he had to go through trials and tribulations for the religion to reach me and you.

297
00:21:46,444 --> 00:21:48,191
We owe Rasool Allah ﷺ a lot,

298
00:21:49,055 --> 00:21:52,563
Rasool Allah ﷺ after mentioning the people of Uhud(أحَد)

299
00:21:53,026 --> 00:21:56,420
then he was giving a Naseeha(نصِيْحَه) to the Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

300
00:21:56,729 --> 00:21:57,277
He told them;

301
00:21:57,341 --> 00:22:04,658
يا معشرَ المهاجِرينَ إنَّكم قَدْ أَصْبَحْتُم تزيدونَ وَ الْأَنْصَارُ عَلَى هَيْئْتِهَا لَا تَزِيْدُ

302
00:22:05,068 --> 00:22:07,316
O, people of Al-Muhajiroon(مهاجرون),

303
00:22:07,356 --> 00:22:09,141
The Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) are the ones, who made Hijrah(هجرة),

304
00:22:09,266 --> 00:22:13,915
you are increasing in numbers while the Ansaar(أنصار) are not increasing in numbers.

305
00:22:14,441 --> 00:22:18,088
That is because the population of Ansaar(أنصار) was the same,

306
00:22:18,256 --> 00:22:21,847
while the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) are increasing because the Hijrah(هجرة) was not only from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

307
00:22:21,879 --> 00:22:24,030
but it was now from all over Arabia.

308
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:28,674
So, the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) are now the majority of the population of Madina.

309
00:22:28,827 --> 00:22:32,227
When in the beginning, the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) were very few in number

310
00:22:32,251 --> 00:22:36,867
and the majority of the people in Madina were the locals, the people of Ansaar(أنصار).

311
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,736
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) that your numbers are adding up

312
00:22:41,028 --> 00:22:43,138
while the Ansaar(أنصار) are not increasing and then he said;

313
00:22:43,163 --> 00:22:48,089
وَاِنَّهُمْ عَيْبَتِيْ الَّتِيْ آوَيْتُ إِلَيْهَا فَأَكْرِمُوْا كَرِيْمَهُمْ وَتَجَاوَزُوْا عَنْ مُسِيْئِهِمْ

314
00:22:48,226 --> 00:22:54,079
They are the ones, who supported me in the beginning so honor the honorable among them,

315
00:22:54,290 --> 00:22:57,002
and forgive the ones among them, who make mistakes.

316
00:22:57,708 --> 00:23:01,534
Rasool Allah ﷺ does not want to die and have the Ansaar(أنصار) suffer

317
00:23:01,959 --> 00:23:04,280
because now they are a minority in Madina.

318
00:23:04,526 --> 00:23:08,222
And Rasool Allah ﷺ is reminding the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) to take care of them,

319
00:23:08,366 --> 00:23:10,808
the good among them, treat them very well.

320
00:23:10,832 --> 00:23:13,101
And the ones among them will make mistakes forgive them.

321
00:23:13,739 --> 00:23:15,284
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

322
00:23:15,628 --> 00:23:22,488
اَيُّهَا النَّاسْ إِنَّ عَبْدًا مِّنْ عِبَادِ اللـه قَدْ خَيَّرَه’ اللـهُ بَيْنَ الدُّنْيَا وَبَيْنَ مَا عِنْدَ اللـه

323
00:23:23,006 --> 00:23:27,110
There is a servant, O people from among the servants of Allah.

324
00:23:27,716 --> 00:23:33,121
And Allah has given him the option of this world or what is in the hands of Allah.

325
00:23:33,743 --> 00:23:38,612
That's all what Rasool Allah ﷺ said. He didn't indicate, who this slave of Allah is.

326
00:23:39,233 --> 00:23:43,410
But Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) understood the meaning and he started to cry.

327
00:23:43,696 --> 00:23:46,693
He understood that Rasool Allah ﷺ is talking about himself

328
00:23:47,290 --> 00:23:50,530
because the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah are given the choice before they die

329
00:23:50,570 --> 00:23:53,872
not like everybody else, the Angel of Death just comes to you unannounced,

330
00:23:54,134 --> 00:23:59,293
the Angel of Death comes to the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) and seeks their permission to take their souls.

331
00:23:59,898 --> 00:24:01,794
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that

332
00:24:01,889 --> 00:24:06,704
there's a slave of Allah, who was given the choice of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) or Akhirah(آخره).

333
00:24:07,177 --> 00:24:09,986
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) cried and he told Rasool Allah ﷺ:

334
00:24:10,019 --> 00:24:12,200
بَلْ نَحْنُ لَفْدِيْكَ بِأَنْفُسِنَا وَاَبْنَائِنَا

335
00:24:12,578 --> 00:24:16,080
We will sacrifice ourselves and our children for you.

336
00:24:16,370 --> 00:24:17,482
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

337
00:24:17,522 --> 00:24:18,298
عَلَى رِسْلِكْ

338
00:24:18,524 --> 00:24:22,533
Rasool Allah ﷺ stopped Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and then told him, he told everyone.

339
00:24:22,881 --> 00:24:24,864
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

340
00:24:24,990 --> 00:24:32,343
The person most faithful to myself in his friendship and his wealth is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

341
00:24:32,935 --> 00:24:40,489
Rasool Allah ﷺ now, towards the end of his life is recognizing Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه in front of everyone

342
00:24:40,529 --> 00:24:44,753
 and letting the people know the status of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

343
00:24:45,075 --> 00:24:50,799
The person, most faithful to myself in his friendship, and his wealth is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

344
00:24:51,194 --> 00:24:57,413
If I were to take any other than Allah, as a beloved one as a Khaleel(خليل), I would so take Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

345
00:24:57,843 --> 00:25:03,609
However, what I do have with him is the companionship of Islam and his love

346
00:25:03,966 --> 00:25:08,113
every door in the mosque should be shut except that of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

347
00:25:09,004 --> 00:25:13,805
Rasool Allah ﷺ said here, Khaleel(خليل), Khaleel(خليل) is a higher level than friend,

348
00:25:13,829 --> 00:25:16,767
it is something that fills your heart with love.

349
00:25:17,116 --> 00:25:22,514
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If I'm going to choose out of this world, a Khaleel(خليل), it would be Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

350
00:25:22,832 --> 00:25:27,693
But I am the Khaleel(خليل) of Allah and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is my brother and friend.

351
00:25:28,061 --> 00:25:31,000
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is the one whom I share with him love.

352
00:25:31,461 --> 00:25:37,412
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave some final advice to the Ummah(امة) in one Hadith(حديث) Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

353
00:25:37,436 --> 00:25:41,013
لَعْنَ الله الْيَهُوْدَ والنَصَارَه اِتَّخَذُوْا قُبُوْرَ الأنْبِيَاءَ مَسَاجِدْ

354
00:25:41,299 --> 00:25:48,067
May Allah curse the Jews and Christians for building Mosques over the graves of their Prophets.

355
00:25:48,757 --> 00:25:51,334
They turned the graves of the prophets into Masajid(مساجد).

356
00:25:51,755 --> 00:25:52,904
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

357
00:25:52,928 --> 00:25:55,764
لَا يبْقَى فِيْ جَزِيْرَةِ الْعَرَبِ دِيْنَانِ

358
00:25:56,017 --> 00:25:59,414
No two religions should coexist in the Arabian Peninsula.

359
00:25:59,829 --> 00:26:05,324
This is a Kuffr(كفر) free zone, the Arabian Peninsula should be purely Islamic.

360
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:11,230
No other religion should coexist with Islam in the Arabian Peninsula.

361
00:26:11,385 --> 00:26:16,159
And this is one of the final words of advice of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

362
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,410
Rasool Allah ﷺ also said;

363
00:26:18,450 --> 00:26:20,130
اُوْصِيْكُمْ بِالصَّلَاةْ

364
00:26:20,532 --> 00:26:23,500
Rasool Allah is giving them the advice of Salah(صلاة).

365
00:26:23,797 --> 00:26:28,671
Rasool Allah ﷺ also gave us advice to take care of the slaves,

366
00:26:28,696 --> 00:26:33,663
Rasool Allah ﷺ repeated this advice to take care of the slaves, to take care of the slaves

367
00:26:34,014 --> 00:26:35,352
and Rasool Allah ﷺ also said;

368
00:26:35,376 --> 00:26:36,671
اِتَّقُوللهَ فِيْ النِسَاء

369
00:26:36,740 --> 00:26:38,005
Fear Allah in the women.

370
00:26:38,045 --> 00:26:44,975
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving the advice to the Ummah(امة), do not take advantage of the weak among the Ummah(امة)

371
00:26:45,795 --> 00:26:46,861
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

372
00:26:46,886 --> 00:26:48,924
مَا تَرَكَ قَوْمٌ الجِهَادْ إِلَّا ذِلُّوا

373
00:26:48,948 --> 00:26:51,677
Whenever people leave Jihad(جهاد), they will be humiliated

374
00:26:52,059 --> 00:26:56,452
and Rasool Allah ﷺ also ordered that the army of Osama(اسامه) should be sent out.

375
00:26:56,523 --> 00:27:00,085
Because now the army of Osama(اسامه) was camping outside the Madina

376
00:27:00,299 --> 00:27:04,628
until, all of the fighters, to get ready, and then they would set out.

377
00:27:04,937 --> 00:27:06,158
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying;

378
00:27:06,182 --> 00:27:07,457
اَنْفِذُوْا بَعَثَ اُسَامَه

379
00:27:07,885 --> 00:27:09,921
Send out the army of Osama(اسامه).

380
00:27:10,467 --> 00:27:14,843
Rasool Allah ﷺ was still going around, the houses of his wives.

381
00:27:15,382 --> 00:27:18,282
But then eventually it was becoming difficult for him.

382
00:27:18,609 --> 00:27:22,392
So, he was carried in to the house of Ayesha(عائشه).

383
00:27:22,782 --> 00:27:25,729
And he gathered all of his wives and he sought their permission

384
00:27:26,078 --> 00:27:32,754
to allow him to stay in the house of Ayesha(عائشه), while he is ill and they agreed.

385
00:27:33,047 --> 00:27:35,871
So, Ayesha(عائشه) had Rasool Allah ﷺ in her house

386
00:27:36,168 --> 00:27:41,942
and she was the one tending to him and she said: This the first time I tended to an ill person.

387
00:27:42,299 --> 00:27:47,759
Rasool Allah ﷺ spent the rest of his life in the house of Ayesha رضي الله عنها,

388
00:27:48,251 --> 00:27:52,086
or the end of his life was in the house of Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

389
00:27:52,483 --> 00:27:57,215
Ayesha(عائشه), she said, that Rasool Allah ﷺ when he would become ill

390
00:27:57,245 --> 00:28:01,273
he would recite the Maoozaat(معؤذات) in his hands

391
00:28:01,297 --> 00:28:03,732
and then he would blow in them and then he would wipe his body.

392
00:28:04,277 --> 00:28:06,761
But when he became ill, he could not do that for himself.

393
00:28:06,790 --> 00:28:11,328
So, Ayesha(عائشه) would recite the Su'arr(سوّر) in the hands of Rasool Ullah

394
00:28:11,437 --> 00:28:15,687
and then she would use his hands to wipe his body for him.

395
00:28:15,934 --> 00:28:20,450
She would not do it, in her own hands, because the hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ are more blessed.

396
00:28:20,909 --> 00:28:27,401
So, even though she would do the recitation, but she would not do it in her hands but in the hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

397
00:28:27,799 --> 00:28:31,791
One day her brother, Abdur Rahman(عبد الرحمن) came in and he had a Miswaak(مسواك).

398
00:28:32,006 --> 00:28:34,155
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was staring at the Miswaak(مسواك),

399
00:28:34,195 --> 00:28:37,131
 so Ayesha(عائشه) understood that Rasool Allah ﷺ wants it.

400
00:28:37,612 --> 00:28:38,953
So, she told him; Do you want it?

401
00:28:38,993 --> 00:28:41,160
 Rasool Allah ﷺ made a gesture that yes.

402
00:28:41,574 --> 00:28:44,902
So she took it from Abdur Rahman(عبد الرحمن) and then she soften the other end,

403
00:28:45,225 --> 00:28:47,008
and she gave it to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

404
00:28:47,048 --> 00:28:50,682
And he used the Miswaak(مسواك), she said: As if he was healthy.

405
00:28:50,906 --> 00:28:54,668
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ, even though he was in the end of his life,

406
00:28:54,693 --> 00:28:57,120
but he was not leaving the Sunnah(سنة) of Miswaak(مسواك).

407
00:28:57,897 --> 00:29:01,741
Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) and the Muslims who were camping out of Madina,

408
00:29:01,765 --> 00:29:05,036
they heard the news of the illness of Rasool Allah ﷺ, so they came back

409
00:29:05,697 --> 00:29:07,833
and Osama(اسامه) came to visit Rasool Allah ﷺ.

410
00:29:07,873 --> 00:29:12,354
And Rasool Ullah was ill to the extent that he could not speak

411
00:29:13,012 --> 00:29:16,076
and then Osama(اسامه) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ raised his hands up

412
00:29:16,437 --> 00:29:19,965
and then he would point to me, he would raise his hands up and then point to me.

413
00:29:20,462 --> 00:29:23,555
Rasool Allah ﷺ was making Dua(دُعَا) for Osama(اسامه).

414
00:29:23,579 --> 00:29:27,791
Osama(اسامه) said: Rasool Ullah, I understood that Rasool Allah ﷺ was making Dua(دُعَا) for me.

415
00:29:27,967 --> 00:29:33,440
Rasool Allah ﷺ was in those difficult moments, the agony and pain of illness.

416
00:29:33,818 --> 00:29:36,526
Nevertheless, he was making the Dua(دُعَا) for Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد)

417
00:29:36,551 --> 00:29:40,783
and this shows us how much Rasool Allah ﷺ loved Osama Bin Zaid رضي الله عنه.

418
00:29:41,232 --> 00:29:44,449
Rasool Allah ﷺ could not go out and lead the Salah(صلاة) anymore.

419
00:29:44,828 --> 00:29:50,454
So, he ordered that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه should lead the Salah(صلاة).

420
00:29:50,716 --> 00:29:52,620
مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ

421
00:29:52,659 --> 00:29:54,675
Order Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to lead the people in Salah(صلاة)

422
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:58,645
Ayesha(عائشه) did not want her father to lead the Salah(صلاة), so she said;

423
00:29:58,954 --> 00:30:02,935
O Rasool Ullah, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is a very soft hearted man.

424
00:30:03,446 --> 00:30:08,352
And I'm afraid that if he stands in your position, he would not be able to handle it

425
00:30:08,392 --> 00:30:10,985
and he will not be able to complete the Salah(صلاة) meaning that

426
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:15,753
if he's in that position, he might become too emotional to continue the Salah(صلاة).

427
00:30:16,531 --> 00:30:17,585
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

428
00:30:17,609 --> 00:30:19,498
 مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاسِ

429
00:30:19,973 --> 00:30:22,473
The objection of Ayesha(عائشه), was repeated again.

430
00:30:22,513 --> 00:30:23,496
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

431
00:30:23,520 --> 00:30:27,246
مُرُوا أَبَا بَكْرٍ فَلْيُصَلِّ بِالنَّاس، إنَّكُنَّ صَوَیحبات يُوسُفَ

432
00:30:27,508 --> 00:30:29,763
You women are the companions of Yusuf(يوسف).

433
00:30:30,072 --> 00:30:36,354
And what Rasool Allah ﷺ meant by that the woman of Yousuf(يوسف) showed something but they were hiding something else.

434
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:41,644
When the wife of Al-Aziz(العزيز) invited all of those women to come,

435
00:30:41,928 --> 00:30:46,013
she invited them Apparently, it is just a gathering.

436
00:30:46,426 --> 00:30:49,807
But in reality, she wanted them there to see Yusuf(يوسف).

437
00:30:50,303 --> 00:30:59,216
And Ayesha رضي الله عنها, her public statement was that my father is a soft hearted man so he won't be able to pray

438
00:30:59,256 --> 00:31:05,151
 but in reality, the reason why she didn't want her father to pray and she actually mentioned that.

439
00:31:05,671 --> 00:31:10,891
she said: The reason I didn't want my father to pray is because people will dislike him

440
00:31:11,441 --> 00:31:13,463
for standing in the place of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

441
00:31:13,503 --> 00:31:16,587
I mean, people were used to having Rasool Allah lead them in Salah(صلاة)

442
00:31:16,809 --> 00:31:22,212
And now they're having somebody else that might make them dislike the fact that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is in that place.

443
00:31:22,370 --> 00:31:24,777
But Rasool Allah ﷺ says in another narration

444
00:31:25,218 --> 00:31:27,923
because it says that Umar رضي الله عنه led the Salah(صلاة).

445
00:31:28,011 --> 00:31:30,678
يأَبَی الله ذَالِكَ وَرَسُولُه’ وَالْمُؤمِنُوْنْ

446
00:31:30,751 --> 00:31:36,410
Allah does not want that and Rasool Allah ﷺ does not want that and the believers, do not want that

447
00:31:36,490 --> 00:31:38,632
it is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who must lead the Muslims in Salah(صلاة)

448
00:31:38,691 --> 00:31:40,096
and this is also an indication that

449
00:31:40,143 --> 00:31:46,031
the Imam(إمام) after Rasool Allah ﷺ is Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكر الصديق) in the issues of religion and in the issues of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

450
00:31:46,671 --> 00:31:53,580
Rasool Allah ﷺ was now extremely tired because of his illness.

451
00:31:54,670 --> 00:31:57,963
And he was not going out to the Salah(صلاة).

452
00:31:58,924 --> 00:32:03,757
But on Monday when the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were Salah(صلاة)

453
00:32:03,781 --> 00:32:07,238
and they were being led by Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

454
00:32:07,831 --> 00:32:12,648
Rasool Allah ﷺ uncovered the curtain that is between him and the Masjid(مسجد).

455
00:32:13,332 --> 00:32:16,229
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) narrates he says and this is Bukhari(بخاريْ).

456
00:32:16,784 --> 00:32:19,856
حتَّى إذَا كانَ يَوْمُ الِاثْنَيْنِ وهُمْ صُفُوفٌ في الصَّلَاةِ

457
00:32:20,423 --> 00:32:23,818
When it was Monday and they were lined up, in Salah(صلاة).

458
00:32:24,401 --> 00:32:27,180
فَكَشَفَ النبيُّ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ سِتْرَ الحُجْرَةِ

459
00:32:27,340 --> 00:32:29,657
Rasool Allah ﷺ uncovered the curtain.

460
00:32:29,935 --> 00:32:34,368
يَنْظُرُ إلَيْنَا وهو قَائِمٌ كَأنَّ وجْهَهُ ورَقَةُ مُصْحَفٍ،

461
00:32:35,274 --> 00:32:38,725
Rasool Allah ﷺ took a look at us and he was standing up

462
00:32:39,112 --> 00:32:43,880
And Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) says; As if his face was a page out of a book.

463
00:32:44,072 --> 00:32:47,608
Meaning clear and clean and beautiful and another narration;

464
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:49,028
كَأنَّ وجْهَهُ فلْقَ الْقَمَرْ

465
00:32:49,345 --> 00:32:51,825
As if his face was part of the moon.

466
00:32:52,816 --> 00:32:54,027
And then Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) said;

467
00:32:54,052 --> 00:32:55,392
ثُمَّ تَبَسَّمَ يَضْحَكُ

468
00:32:55,416 --> 00:32:57,774
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing.

469
00:32:58,630 --> 00:33:02,677
فَهَمَمْنَا أنْ نَفْتَتِنَ مِنَ الفَرَحِ برُؤْيَةِ النبيِّ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ

470
00:33:02,702 --> 00:33:08,655
It was almost going to be a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for us because of our happiness, by seeing Rasool Allah ﷺ.

471
00:33:08,679 --> 00:33:11,741
What he meant by Fitnah(فِتْنَه) is, that we were going to walk out of Salah(صلاة)

472
00:33:12,205 --> 00:33:17,788
because we were in Salah(صلاة) and we saw that, and it is so beautiful and so much joy for us,

473
00:33:18,007 --> 00:33:19,645
we're almost going to lose our Salah(صلاة).

474
00:33:20,243 --> 00:33:25,642
And Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was coming back, so that Rasool Allah ﷺ would lead the Salah(صلاة),

475
00:33:25,829 --> 00:33:29,676
but Rasool Allah ﷺ had, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) pray in his place.

476
00:33:30,481 --> 00:33:34,468
However, Rasool Allah ﷺ did come out at a certain time

477
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:38,976
and He would sit down, but Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) would be standing up.

478
00:33:39,001 --> 00:33:42,569
And some narration say that it was actually Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) leading the Salah(صلاة)

479
00:33:42,870 --> 00:33:45,775
but others say that it was Rasool Ullah leading Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

480
00:33:46,037 --> 00:33:48,296
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was standing and leading the rest.

481
00:33:49,097 --> 00:33:52,037
Back to this narration of Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه,

482
00:33:52,600 --> 00:33:59,372
 he said that the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he saw them, he was smiling with joy. Why?

483
00:34:00,118 --> 00:34:05,469
And by the way, this is the last scene that Rasool Allah ﷺ sees from his Ummah(امة),

484
00:34:06,215 --> 00:34:09,156
the last thing that Rasool Allah ﷺ saw, from his Ummah(امة)

485
00:34:09,672 --> 00:34:12,468
was them in Salah(صلاة), in Salaah-Tul-Jama'ah(صلاة الجماعة).

486
00:34:13,082 --> 00:34:17,766
Brothers and sisters, when you are praying to Allahعَزّوجَلّ

487
00:34:18,542 --> 00:34:21,977
and for the brothers whom Salaah-Tul-Jama'ah(صلاة الجماعة) is Wajib(واجب) on them.

488
00:34:22,824 --> 00:34:29,486
When you are in Salaah-Tul-Jama'a(صلاة الجماعة), this is a site that pleases Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

489
00:34:29,848 --> 00:34:32,404
When Rasool Allah ﷺ uncovered that curtain.

490
00:34:33,113 --> 00:34:37,702
He saw the result, he saw the fruit of his effort and his Daw'ah(دعوة).

491
00:34:38,456 --> 00:34:43,726
The Muslims are lining up in Salah(صلاة) the most important deed in Islam after

492
00:34:43,750 --> 00:34:46,711
أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًارَسُولُ الله  ‫‬

493
00:34:47,200 --> 00:34:53,676
And Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled with happiness, because Rasool Allah ﷺ was now seen standing up,

494
00:34:54,176 --> 00:34:57,764
they assumed that the Rasool Allah ﷺ has become better.

495
00:34:58,173 --> 00:35:02,477
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) sought permission to go to As-Sun'hh(ألصنح),

496
00:35:02,816 --> 00:35:08,429
where his other wife was, which was a little bit outside of Madina

497
00:35:08,804 --> 00:35:13,029
because he was tied up in Madina due to the illness of Rasool Allah ﷺ

498
00:35:13,069 --> 00:35:15,899
but now he thought that Rasool Allah ﷺ is better, so he left.

499
00:35:16,591 --> 00:35:22,914
And Al-Abbas(العباس), he met Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) after he came out from the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

500
00:35:23,217 --> 00:35:27,728
And this is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ), He met with Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and he told him;

501
00:35:28,066 --> 00:35:30,842
يَا أبَا لْحَسَنٍ، كيفَ أصْبَحَ رَسولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ؟

502
00:35:31,057 --> 00:35:33,192
How is Rasool Allah ﷺ doing, this morning.?

503
00:35:33,788 --> 00:35:35,082
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

504
00:35:35,106 --> 00:35:36,800
أصْبَحَ بحَمْدِ اللَّهِ بَارِئًا

505
00:35:37,112 --> 00:35:39,590
He looks with the praise of Allah much better.

506
00:35:40,317 --> 00:35:43,505
Al-Abbas(العباس) grabbed the hand of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and told him;

507
00:35:43,608 --> 00:35:45,937
أنْتَ واللَّهِ بَعْدَ ثَلَاثٍ عبدُ العَصَا

508
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:50,817
After three days from now, you would be a slave ruled by a stick.

509
00:35:51,101 --> 00:35:53,958
What does Al-Abbas(العباس) mean by this, you would be a slave ruled by a stick,

510
00:35:53,982 --> 00:35:56,828
meaning that you would be a person without any authority.

511
00:35:58,254 --> 00:36:00,389
You would be a follower, without any authority.

512
00:36:00,799 --> 00:36:04,160
And this is Farasah(فراسه) of Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه.

513
00:36:04,422 --> 00:36:05,670
Farasah(فراسه) is intuition.

514
00:36:06,007 --> 00:36:06,961
Al-Abbas(العباس) said;

515
00:36:07,215 --> 00:36:12,097
إنِّي وَلله لَأَعْرِفُ اَلْمَوْتْ فِيْ وُجُوهِ بَنِي عبدِ المُطَّلِب

516
00:36:12,605 --> 00:36:17,485
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: I can read death in the faces of the sons of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).

517
00:36:17,673 --> 00:36:19,804
And I can see death in the face of Rasool Ullah,

518
00:36:19,886 --> 00:36:21,918
everybody was thinking that Rasool Allah was better.

519
00:36:22,092 --> 00:36:23,115
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: No.

520
00:36:23,478 --> 00:36:27,687
I recognize death in my family, I can see it, in their faces.

521
00:36:27,824 --> 00:36:30,586
And I can actually see it now in the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

522
00:36:30,754 --> 00:36:33,615
And I think that Rasool Ullah would die pretty soon.

523
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:38,179
Al-Abbas(العباس) doesn't know the unseen, death is something that only Allah knows.

524
00:36:38,410 --> 00:36:42,118
But Al-Abbas(العباس) has this intuition, where he could recognize

525
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:45,582
when the sons of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) are approaching their death.

526
00:36:46,001 --> 00:36:47,381
So, he told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب);

527
00:36:47,698 --> 00:36:49,817
Go and ask Rasool Allah ﷺ,

528
00:36:50,006 --> 00:36:54,625
if we are going to be in authority of the Ummah(امة) after him.

529
00:36:54,919 --> 00:36:57,189
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) refused and he said;

530
00:36:57,602 --> 00:37:05,683
I will not ask him that because if he rejects that, then the Ummah(أمة) will not give it to us, to the end of time.

531
00:37:05,987 --> 00:37:09,729
And Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) refused to go and talk to Rasool Allah ﷺ about this.

532
00:37:10,811 --> 00:37:16,230
Anyway, there was a very steep deterioration in the situation of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

533
00:37:16,474 --> 00:37:19,947
And within that day, that same day, which is Monday now,

534
00:37:20,155 --> 00:37:24,327
Rasool Allah ﷺ has been ill now, for about 13 days,

535
00:37:24,956 --> 00:37:28,417
Rasool Allah ﷺ started going through Saqraat-Ul-Maot(سقراة الموت).

536
00:37:29,663 --> 00:37:34,726
Saqraat-Ul-Maot(سقراة الموت) are the final moments, the agony of death, when the soul is coming out.

537
00:37:35,588 --> 00:37:41,294
So, Ayesha(عائشه) brought some water for Rasool Allah and he would soak a piece of cloth in that water,

538
00:37:41,517 --> 00:37:44,656
 and then he would wipe his face with it and say;

539
00:37:44,981 --> 00:37:46,974
اِنَّ لِلْمَوْتِ لَسَكرَاتْ

540
00:37:47,346 --> 00:37:50,170
There's agony in death, there's agony in death.

541
00:37:50,846 --> 00:37:55,775
Rasool Allah ﷺ himself, the best of the creation have to go through this.

542
00:37:56,146 --> 00:37:59,312
And he was in the lap of Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

543
00:37:59,817 --> 00:38:07,856
And Ayesha(عائشه) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ looked up towards the roof with his eyes.

544
00:38:08,559 --> 00:38:09,464
And I heard him say;

545
00:38:09,489 --> 00:38:13,918
بَلِّ الرَّفيقَ الأَعْلى، بَلِّ الرَّفيقَ الأَعْلى، بَلِّ الرَّفيقَ الأَعْلى

546
00:38:14,508 --> 00:38:20,172
No! The highest companion, the highest companion, the highest companion,

547
00:38:20,915 --> 00:38:26,409
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said: I knew that Rasool Allah ﷺ was being asked by the angel of death,

548
00:38:26,898 --> 00:38:29,434
whether he wants to stay with us or to leave.

549
00:38:29,891 --> 00:38:34,916
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying: I want to be with the highest companion, and that is Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

550
00:38:35,764 --> 00:38:39,861
And then Ayesha(عائشه) says; The head of Rasool Allah ﷺ turned towards me.

551
00:38:40,763 --> 00:38:44,420
And she screamed, in the narration of Ibn Hishaam(إبن هشام);

552
00:38:45,005 --> 00:38:46,620
وَمِنْ حمقي وَقِلَّة عَقْلِيْ

553
00:38:46,644 --> 00:38:50,413
Because of my foolishness, I screamed, and I yelled

554
00:38:50,620 --> 00:38:55,608
and now the news spreading around Madina like fire.

555
00:38:56,519 --> 00:39:01,883
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه and Al-Mugheerah(المغيره) rushed in into the room

556
00:39:02,418 --> 00:39:03,676
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

557
00:39:04,087 --> 00:39:06,471
مَا اَشَدّ مَا غَشِيَّ عَلَيْهْ

558
00:39:07,123 --> 00:39:11,061
Rasool Allah ﷺ is unconsciousness, and this is severe unconsciousness.

559
00:39:12,167 --> 00:39:16,041
And when they were walking out Al-Mugheerah(المغيره) told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب);

560
00:39:16,553 --> 00:39:18,696
لَقَدْ تُوُّفِيَّ رَسُولُ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

561
00:39:18,744 --> 00:39:20,025
Rasool Allah ﷺ is dead.

562
00:39:20,688 --> 00:39:23,363
This is not unconsciousness, Rasool Allah ﷺ is dead.

563
00:39:23,783 --> 00:39:27,867
You know, brothers and sisters, we cannot imagine how this news was on the Sahabah(صحابه)

564
00:39:28,223 --> 00:39:31,019
because we don't have that same love.

565
00:39:31,503 --> 00:39:35,729
We did not live with Rasool Allah ﷺ for years.

566
00:39:36,178 --> 00:39:38,380
Rasool Allah ﷺ for them was everything.

567
00:39:38,642 --> 00:39:42,832
He was their leader, he was like their father to them.

568
00:39:43,268 --> 00:39:46,604
He was an advisor to them, he was their teacher, he was everything.

569
00:39:47,232 --> 00:39:52,099
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he heard, Al-Mugheerah(المغيره) say, that Rasool Allah ﷺ died.

570
00:39:52,415 --> 00:39:53,434
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

571
00:39:53,459 --> 00:39:55,324
اِنَّكَ رَجُلٌ تَحُوْسُكَ فِتْنَه

572
00:39:55,348 --> 00:40:00,493
You are a man of Fitnah(فِتْنَه) or you are a man who wants to bring dissension among the Ummah(امة).

573
00:40:01,329 --> 00:40:06,614
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not die because he will not die until the exterminate the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

574
00:40:06,961 --> 00:40:09,795
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) understood that Rasool Allah ﷺ will not die

575
00:40:09,820 --> 00:40:11,452
until all of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) are killed.

576
00:40:11,831 --> 00:40:14,414
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) rushed out to the Masjid(مسجد)

577
00:40:14,831 --> 00:40:19,418
and the people were starting to come in crowds in the Masjid(مسجد) and there was weeping everywhere.

578
00:40:19,608 --> 00:40:23,715
Everyone was crying, and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) drew out his sword and said;

579
00:40:24,151 --> 00:40:28,280
there are some Munafiqeen(منافقين), who are claiming that Rasool Allah ﷺ died.

580
00:40:28,692 --> 00:40:34,600
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not die but Rasool Allah ﷺ is unconscious like Musa(موسى) became unconscious,

581
00:40:34,800 --> 00:40:37,647
and he will come back and he will kill all of the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

582
00:40:37,745 --> 00:40:40,269
And whoever says that Rasool Allah ﷺ is dead,

583
00:40:40,500 --> 00:40:43,081
I'm going to cut off his head with the sword of mine.

584
00:40:43,695 --> 00:40:49,812
The news reached Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه and he came back from As-Sun'hh(ألصنح) on his horse.

585
00:40:50,367 --> 00:40:54,328
And he did not speak to anyonen and he came into the room of Ayesha(عائشه).

586
00:40:55,102 --> 00:40:58,316
With Rasool Allah ﷺ covered with cloth.

587
00:40:58,458 --> 00:41:04,297
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه uncovered the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ and when he saw him, he cried.

588
00:41:05,012 --> 00:41:07,342
And then he kissed Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

589
00:41:07,673 --> 00:41:12,471
You are pure, when alive and you are a pure when dead.

590
00:41:13,132 --> 00:41:16,538
In the name of Allah, Allah will not make you die twice.

591
00:41:17,277 --> 00:41:23,781
And the death that was prescribed on you, the death that is ordained on you and everybody else, you have went through it.

592
00:41:24,356 --> 00:41:25,499
 So, now that's it.

593
00:41:25,986 --> 00:41:28,946
You have went through the death that's prescribed on you.

594
00:41:29,247 --> 00:41:33,743
And then Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) came out of the room of Ayesha(عائشه) and went to the Masjid(مسجد)

595
00:41:34,297 --> 00:41:38,372
and, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) a was screaming and yelling and threatening.

596
00:41:38,814 --> 00:41:40,739
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكر الصديق), told Umar(عمر),

597
00:41:40,763 --> 00:41:41,792
إِجْلِسْ يَا عُمر

598
00:41:41,816 --> 00:41:44,630
sit down Umar(عمر)! Umar(عمر) ignored Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

599
00:41:45,068 --> 00:41:50,092
He told him, sit down Umar(عمر)! A second time and Umar(عمر) is carrying on.

600
00:41:50,386 --> 00:41:53,170
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) then, started speaking

601
00:41:53,489 --> 00:42:01,231
and people just left Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and came to listen to, what Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had to say.

602
00:42:02,462 --> 00:42:03,812
Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه said;

603
00:42:04,160 --> 00:42:11,489
مَن كانَ يَعْبُدُ مُحَمَّدًا فإنَّ مُحَمَّدًا قدْ مَاتَ، ومَن كانَ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ فإنَّ اللَّهَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوتُ

604
00:42:12,344 --> 00:42:15,978
Whoever used to worship Muhammad(محمد), then know that Muhammad(محمد) is dead,

605
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:22,708
and whoever used to worship Allah, then know that Allah is alive and he would never die.

606
00:42:23,306 --> 00:42:24,919
And then he recited the Ayah(آية).

607
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:39,519
وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ ۚ أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَىٰ أَعْقَابِكُمْۚ

608
00:42:39,662 --> 00:42:50,403
وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلَىٰ عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئًا ۗ وَسَيَجْزِي اللَّهُ الشَّاكِرِينَ۝

609
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:55,491
Muhammad(محمد) is not, but a Messenger, other Messengers have passed on before him.

610
00:42:55,995 --> 00:43:02,668
So, if he was to die or be killed would you turn back on your heels, to unbelief

611
00:43:02,924 --> 00:43:09,046
and he, who turns back on his heels, will never harm Allah at all but Allah will reward, the Grateful.

612
00:43:09,665 --> 00:43:12,466
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Is this Ayah(آية) in the book of Allah.

613
00:43:13,128 --> 00:43:15,295
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) already knows the Ayah(آية)

614
00:43:15,691 --> 00:43:19,147
 but Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), it is, as if he heard it, for the first time.

615
00:43:19,925 --> 00:43:24,311
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I realized that Muhammadﷺ was dead.

616
00:43:24,823 --> 00:43:27,314
فَعَقَرْتْ فَمَا تَكِلِّنِيْ رَجِلَيْكْ

617
00:43:27,803 --> 00:43:32,267
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) collapsed and said my feet cannot carry me anymore.

618
00:43:33,552 --> 00:43:39,160
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) the strong, powerful man could not handle the news,

619
00:43:39,184 --> 00:43:41,243
it was like an arrow that struck his heart,

620
00:43:41,606 --> 00:43:46,034
and he fell down because his knees could not carry him anymore.

621
00:43:47,171 --> 00:43:48,919
And the narrators says;

622
00:43:49,017 --> 00:43:51,571
فَمَا سمع بَشَرٌمِّنَّ النَّاسِ اِلَّا يَتْلُوْهَا

623
00:43:51,696 --> 00:43:55,913
Everyone was reciting this Ayah(آية), as if they heard it for the first time.

624
00:43:56,440 --> 00:44:01,077
We will skip the event of the Bay'yah(بيعة) to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)

625
00:44:01,191 --> 00:44:06,437
because I already talked about it, in the beginning of the lectures on Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق).

626
00:44:06,746 --> 00:44:11,400
We'll move on to the washing of Rasool Allah ﷺ and how, his burial?

627
00:44:12,389 --> 00:44:17,690
Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه said that the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ

628
00:44:18,288 --> 00:44:23,122
are the ones, who took care of the washing of the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ

629
00:44:23,551 --> 00:44:25,527
 and those were Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس ابن عبد المطلب)

630
00:44:25,599 --> 00:44:28,925
and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and Fazal Bin Abbas(فضل بن عاس), Kizm Bin Al-Abbas(كظم بن عباس)

631
00:44:29,622 --> 00:44:35,340
and Osama Bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) and Salih(صالح) the servant of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

632
00:44:35,730 --> 00:44:40,011
And then Aos Bin Khaoli(أوس بن خولي), one of Ansaar(أنْصَار) he knocked on the door

633
00:44:40,036 --> 00:44:43,230
and told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), I ask you in the name Allah to allow me in.

634
00:44:43,270 --> 00:44:47,055
So, he was allowed in, but he did not participated in the actual washing.

635
00:44:47,614 --> 00:44:51,107
Ali(علي) had the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ, on his chest.

636
00:44:51,891 --> 00:44:58,717
And it is said, in a narration that they were debating whether to wash Rasool Allah ﷺ with his clothes or without his clothes

637
00:44:58,772 --> 00:45:01,165
 because the Sunnah(سنة) is to wash without the clothes.

638
00:45:01,667 --> 00:45:04,878
But then they heard a sound telling them to wash Rasool Ullah with his clothes.

639
00:45:04,988 --> 00:45:09,388
So, the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ was not uncovered, during his washing.

640
00:45:09,517 --> 00:45:12,962
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: We washed him, from over his garments.

641
00:45:13,349 --> 00:45:19,622
And  Al-Abbas(العباس), Fazal(فضل) and Kizam(كظم) used to turn the body around for, with Ali(علي)

642
00:45:19,840 --> 00:45:23,721
and Usama bin Zaid(اسامه بن زيد) and Saleh(صالح) the servant of Rasool Ullah were the ones pouring the water.

643
00:45:23,961 --> 00:45:28,516
And Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was the one, who would rub the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

644
00:45:28,802 --> 00:45:33,022
And then, they put him in three pieces of cloth which were the shroud,

645
00:45:33,536 --> 00:45:36,694
that was the shroud of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

646
00:45:37,020 --> 00:45:40,527
The Salah(صلاة) of Janazah(جنازه) on Rasool Allah ﷺ, it wasn't one congregation

647
00:45:40,567 --> 00:45:43,131
 but people would come in and pray and then they would come out.

648
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:48,574
And this carried on, men would come in and out as much as the room would fit.

649
00:45:48,785 --> 00:45:52,041
making Salah-Janazah(صلاة جنازه) on Rasool Allah ﷺ.

650
00:45:52,900 --> 00:45:59,604
And the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ was in the room of Ayesha رضي الله عنها.

651
00:45:59,946 --> 00:46:04,513
And Umm Salamah(أم سلمه) says: We were all together, the women of Rasool Ullah crying,

652
00:46:04,906 --> 00:46:10,060
and we had the little comfort in seeing, at least the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

653
00:46:10,084 --> 00:46:16,405
even if Rasool Allah was not alive, we had the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ to look at, with us in the room,

654
00:46:16,706 --> 00:46:19,015
 and we are crying, continuously crying.

655
00:46:19,636 --> 00:46:24,666
And then Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), she said and this is Wednesday night, late at night.

656
00:46:25,396 --> 00:46:29,549
She said: We heard the pickaxes, we heard the digging,

657
00:46:30,231 --> 00:46:32,391
the digging of the grave of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

658
00:46:32,416 --> 00:46:36,753
We all broke down and screamed and they heard it in the Masjid(مسجد)

659
00:46:36,778 --> 00:46:40,613
and they screamed and all of Madina, there was an uproar in all of Madina.

660
00:46:41,332 --> 00:46:45,841
Because now they know that the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ is going into His grave.

661
00:46:46,454 --> 00:46:48,616
She said: They heard us, in the Masjid(مسجد)

662
00:46:48,656 --> 00:46:52,311
and then from the Masjid(مسجد), the crying was everywhere all over Madina.

663
00:46:52,569 --> 00:46:56,023
And when it was time for Fajar(فجر) Bilal(بلال) was making Azaan(اذان).

664
00:46:56,440 --> 00:46:59,215
He said: Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر)

665
00:46:59,247 --> 00:47:02,481
اشهدوالله اله الا الله ،, اشهدوالله اله الا الله

666
00:47:02,672 --> 00:47:03,310
And when he came to

667
00:47:03,342 --> 00:47:04,591
اشهد اَنَّ محمد رسول الله

668
00:47:04,615 --> 00:47:08,343
And he could not go any further, he started crying and could not finish the Azaan(اذان).

669
00:47:09,081 --> 00:47:13,332
So, they dug the grave of Rasool Allah ﷺ in the room of Ayesha(عائشه),

670
00:47:13,653 --> 00:47:19,171
according to the Sunnah(سنه), that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are buried in the place where they died

671
00:47:19,691 --> 00:47:25,552
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was buried in the room of Ayesha رضي الله عنه.

672
00:47:25,877 --> 00:47:34,185
Ayesha(عائشه) said, that she saw a dream that three moons fell in her lap.

673
00:47:34,445 --> 00:47:37,648
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) and he was very good at dream interpretations.

674
00:47:38,393 --> 00:47:48,083
He said: If your dream is true, then three men from the best men on the face of the earth, would be buried in your house.

675
00:47:48,519 --> 00:47:51,161
And when it was time to burry Rasool Allah ﷺ.

676
00:47:51,201 --> 00:47:55,992
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told Ayesha رضي الله عنها this is the best of your moons.

677
00:47:56,633 --> 00:48:01,315
The body of Rasool Allah ﷺ was descended into the grave

678
00:48:01,339 --> 00:48:05,929
and again it was the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ that took care of his burial.

679
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:11,850
However, it says in one narration, that Al-Mugheerah(المغيره) before they would cover the grave.

680
00:48:12,126 --> 00:48:15,590
He threw in, his ring intentionally into the grave.

681
00:48:15,899 --> 00:48:19,797
And then he told everyone, wait, wait, let me go and grab my ring.

682
00:48:19,837 --> 00:48:25,651
So, he went down to the grave to be the last person, who would touch Rasool Allah ﷺ, and then it came out.

683
00:48:25,992 --> 00:48:29,752
When the burial was done and people came back.

684
00:48:30,149 --> 00:48:32,188
Fatima رضي الله عنها said: يَا اَنَسْ

685
00:48:32,268 --> 00:48:33,872
She is speaking to Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك), she said;

686
00:48:33,938 --> 00:48:37,843
يا أنَسُ أطَابَتْ أنْفُسُكُمْ أنْ تَحفی التُّرَابَ علَى رَسولِ اللَّهِ

687
00:48:38,394 --> 00:48:44,705
Did your heart allow you to throw dirt on the body of Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was buried.

688
00:48:45,135 --> 00:48:47,646
So, the whole thing was difficult for them,

689
00:48:47,671 --> 00:48:50,635
the washing of Rasool Ullah, the burial of Rasool Ullah, the death of Rasool Ullah,

690
00:48:51,069 --> 00:48:54,042
everything was it was very difficult on the Ummah(امة).

691
00:48:54,389 --> 00:48:56,310
And that's why, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

692
00:48:56,334 --> 00:49:00,773
Whenever a calamity befalls one of you, remember the calamity of my death,

693
00:49:01,261 --> 00:49:06,261
the greatest calamity that can befall a Muslim has already happened,

694
00:49:06,341 --> 00:49:11,241
and that is the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ, whatever happens to you after that is going to be small

695
00:49:11,879 --> 00:49:14,620
compared to the loss of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

696
00:49:15,007 --> 00:49:17,597
compared to the fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ is not with us.

697
00:49:17,901 --> 00:49:19,178
Everything else is small.

698
00:49:19,498 --> 00:49:23,001
And there was Fitnah(فتنه) after the death of Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

699
00:49:23,528 --> 00:49:25,687
Many of the tribes became Murtadd(مرتد).

700
00:49:26,163 --> 00:49:27,562
Muhammad Ibn Is'haaq(إسحاق محمد ابن) says;

701
00:49:27,647 --> 00:49:30,511
وَلَمَّا توُفِّيَ رسولُ اللَّهِ صلَّى اللَّهُ عليهِ وسلَّمَ ارتدَّتِ العربُ

702
00:49:31,031 --> 00:49:32,721
The Arabs became apostate.

703
00:49:32,827 --> 00:49:34,846
وَاشْرَأَبّتْ الْيَهُودِيّةُ والنصرانية

704
00:49:35,022 --> 00:49:38,310
And Jews and Christians started showing themselves again.

705
00:49:38,596 --> 00:49:39,530
وَنَجَمَ النّفَاقُ

706
00:49:39,581 --> 00:49:41,855
And hypocrisy became very widespread.

707
00:49:42,219 --> 00:49:46,527
وَصَارَ الْمُسْلِمُونَ كَالْغَنَمِ الْمَطِيرَةُ فِي اللّيْلَةِ الشّاتِيَةِ لِفَقْدِ نَبِيّهِمْ

708
00:49:46,734 --> 00:49:53,450
And Muslims were like lost sheep in a cold rainy night after the Prophet Rasool Allah ﷺ died,

709
00:49:53,635 --> 00:49:55,937
حَتّى جَمَعَهُمْ اللهُ عَلَى أَبِي بَكْرٍالصديق

710
00:49:55,962 --> 00:49:59,563
Until they were brought together again, under Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

711
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:04,718
And Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه says: I witnessed two days in my life.

712
00:50:04,878 --> 00:50:08,173
One of them was the best day and one of them was the worst day.

713
00:50:08,607 --> 00:50:12,706
The best day was the day when Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Madina.

714
00:50:12,968 --> 00:50:15,430
And that was a day when everything was bright.

715
00:50:16,060 --> 00:50:20,589
And then the worst day was the day Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away and that was a dark day.

716
00:50:21,036 --> 00:50:22,187
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) also says;

717
00:50:22,211 --> 00:50:25,618
ومَا نَفَذنَا عَنْ رسولِ اللَّهِ صلَّى اللَّهُ عليْهِ وسلَّمَ اَلْأَيْدِيَ حَتَّى أنْكَرْنَا قُلُوْبَنَا

718
00:50:25,903 --> 00:50:30,070
By the time we were dusting our hands after the burial of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

719
00:50:30,094 --> 00:50:32,156
we would already feel that our hearts are different.

720
00:50:32,573 --> 00:50:37,199
The hearts were different because of death of Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

721
00:50:38,121 --> 00:50:42,228
One day Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عمر) decided to visit Umm Aimen(ام ايمن).

722
00:50:42,873 --> 00:50:46,587
She started to cry and they told her, Why are you crying?

723
00:50:46,611 --> 00:50:49,465
She said: I'm crying because there is no more revelation.

724
00:50:50,325 --> 00:50:52,967
So, it was not only Rasool Allah ﷺ that, they were missing

725
00:50:53,007 --> 00:50:56,639
but they were also missing the revelation that was coming from As-Samawaat(أسماواة).

726
00:50:56,664 --> 00:50:59,544
I mean, imagine living in a time when Qur'an was being revealed,

727
00:50:59,923 --> 00:51:03,598
Ayaat(آيات) you're going to hear for the first time in your life.

728
00:51:03,899 --> 00:51:05,956
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ leave behind?

729
00:51:06,297 --> 00:51:10,066
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not leave behind any inheritance.

730
00:51:10,422 --> 00:51:12,463
Rasool Allah ﷺ lived for his Ummah(امة).

731
00:51:12,923 --> 00:51:19,536
Lived, serving Allahعَزّوجَلّ and Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away from this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) clean.

732
00:51:20,438 --> 00:51:25,216
He only left behind a white Mule and his weapons

733
00:51:25,501 --> 00:51:32,174
and a land that he left behind for the travelers, as Sadaqah(صدقه), that's all what Rasool Allah ﷺ had.

734
00:51:32,724 --> 00:51:37,203
His arms, which he used to fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) and that's it.

735
00:51:37,800 --> 00:51:43,940
No property, no land, no wealth, no gold and no silver, A Mule and arms.

736
00:51:44,161 --> 00:51:51,598
Muhammad Ibn Is'haq(إسحاق محمد ابن) says: Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away on the 12th of Rabi-Ul-Awwal(ربيع اول).

737
00:51:51,973 --> 00:51:56,451
same day in which he made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina, 10 years ago.

738
00:51:57,096 --> 00:52:01,620
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ lived for exactly 10 years, in Madina.

739
00:52:02,015 --> 00:52:05,001
Rasool Allah ﷺ died at the age of 63,

740
00:52:05,312 --> 00:52:11,343
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) died at the age of 63, and Umar(عمر) died at the age of 63.

741
00:52:11,546 --> 00:52:15,509
They followed the footsteps of Rasool Ullah even in his death.

742
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:22,777
Brothers and sisters, this is the end of the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

743
00:52:23,297 --> 00:52:28,631
We thank Allahعَزّوجَلّ, we say, Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله, ألحمدلله, ألحمدلله)

744
00:52:29,182 --> 00:52:37,662
who allowed us to go through the life, the Seerah(سيرة) of the best of creation, Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

745
00:52:38,367 --> 00:52:43,621
It is a wonderful time to spend with the story of our beloved Prophet.

746
00:52:43,917 --> 00:52:47,304
So, we asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ, dear brothers and sisters in the end

747
00:52:47,851 --> 00:52:50,510
to make us of those, who love Rasool Allah ﷺ,

748
00:52:51,155 --> 00:52:53,964
to make us of those who truly love Rasool Allah ﷺ,

749
00:52:54,643 --> 00:52:57,416
to make us of those, who will follow his Sunnah(سنة), his way.

750
00:52:57,987 --> 00:53:03,877
And to the make us of those, who would be raised up with him on the day of judgment

751
00:53:04,647 --> 00:53:08,002
and will drink from his hands, from Al-Kausar(ألكوثر).

752
00:53:08,627 --> 00:53:12,800
We asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ to admit us with him into paradise.

753
00:53:13,214 --> 00:53:18,485
Brothers and sisters, review the seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, hear it again.

754
00:53:18,782 --> 00:53:25,915
Follow it and love Muhammadﷺ, and be concerned about the Ummah(امة),

755
00:53:26,192 --> 00:53:28,665
like Rasool Allah ﷺ was concerned about the Ummah(امة).

756
00:53:29,224 --> 00:53:32,419
Remember that Rasool Allah ﷺ lived and died for you.

757
00:53:32,962 --> 00:53:42,009
Remember that Rasool Allah ﷺ, left a lot of the enjoyment of the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) for the sake of having Islam come to you

758
00:53:42,605 --> 00:53:46,517
 and say Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدالله) about that and be grateful, be grateful.

759
00:53:46,877 --> 00:53:50,750
The one who is not grateful towards people, will not be grateful towards Allah.

760
00:53:51,387 --> 00:53:57,069
And who among all humanity do we owe more to than Rasool Allah ﷺ,

761
00:53:57,518 --> 00:53:59,655
we owe a lot to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

762
00:54:00,268 --> 00:54:03,367
Everything that we know about Islam came to us through him.

763
00:54:03,691 --> 00:54:07,037
How much do we owe to Rasool Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

764
00:54:07,494 --> 00:54:14,073
The least that we could do in recognition for what Rasool Allah ﷺ did for us, is that we follow him

765
00:54:14,343 --> 00:54:19,091
 and make Salah(صلاة) and Salaam(سلام) on Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

766
00:54:19,296 --> 00:54:25,735
اَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ علَى مُحَمَّدٍ وعلَى آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ، كَمَا صَلَّيْتَ علَى آلِ إبْرَاهِيمَ

767
00:54:26,106 --> 00:54:35,607
وَ بَارِكْ علَى مُحَمَّدٍ وعلَى آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ، كَمَا بَارَكْتَ علَى إبْرَاهِيمَ، وعلَى آلِ إبْرَاهِيمَ إنَّكَ حَمِيدٌ مَجِيدٌ

768
00:54:36,519 --> 00:54:39,302
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

